{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9374c8ebd874686b5edc82805c878cb","id":"pg_4ddad41dd11b5273aab13d7dc9628311","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openhands-openhands-readme-windows-md-28464621d879-3d7dc9628311.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_231aca3831ce5f3280e599d39e57591a"],"title":"OpenHands/OpenHands/README.windows.md @ 28464621d879","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9374c8ebd874686b5edc82805c878cb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_08c1442c8ba39b44ad195fc4f799f82db630b67adde1d4462d9faa7388cc4a99"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Running without a sandbox executes the agent-server directly on the host, where the agent has full filesystem access; the Docker option restricts agent access to projects under PROJECTS_PATH."},{"claim_ids":["clm_117813620b870bc6441ccc1278877749b78300ab93e19feb74cb46c736d9a13f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Non-sandboxed installs require Node.js 22.12.x or later and uv; the Docker option requires Docker Desktop or Engine and a PROJECTS_PATH host directory."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3eb5905676aaa9b01f870acc7cba1c41ecaa6ebe95979991b3cdde6d7184b29b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent Canvas is described as a self-hosted developer control center for coding agents and automations, currently in beta status."},{"claim_ids":["clm_49c25e9e4c714aa8c5ff0386c2b77d3f42de2833fc38028ce18331f7420d7917"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The UI is served at localhost:8000 for npm/source launches and at /canvas for the Docker image, with backends addable from the UI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ab89b3e6f087705482b6c66f6b7487d2acc55f07efc9bd120e7e31a254b1fd25"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Agent Canvas is powered by the OpenHands Agent Server, a REST API for running multiple agents on one machine; the frontend can connect to and switch between multiple Agent Servers."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b102b6fbf0dd73b87495b80b328e6fd09ac258d037bc803aa0c14527fd5e220d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is split across repositories: this repo owns the frontend, backend selection, and local-stack orchestration, while the SDK owns the Agent Server API and the automation repo owns scheduling and dispatching."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b5778ec096c8aedf70bda1d8e9768c89805135737f4f2341627da89487741738"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent-canvas CLI starts the full local stack by default and supports --frontend-only and --backend-only flags to run pieces separately."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c4e24fcc04fef0d130e6b37aaa2389bbdbb1304395e66cd59b6820e67fe33d80"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are directed to AGENTS.md for contributor-specific repository boundaries and a required custom code-review guide."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f1c91aec83a0e9718c944ae4ea5faa2012761c4654b0ee3e5d2bc82d01b4a720"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"An Automation Server can be paired with the Agent Server to run agents on a schedule or in response to events, dispatching conversations to the Agent Server/SDK."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fc6129a93846711e98cfe1c967e72301cac361acb4a3e2253bf8319653df7d71"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"It can run OpenHands, Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, or any ACP-compatible agent across local, remote, and cloud backends."}],"claim_ids":["clm_08c1442c8ba39b44ad195fc4f799f82db630b67adde1d4462d9faa7388cc4a99","clm_117813620b870bc6441ccc1278877749b78300ab93e19feb74cb46c736d9a13f","clm_3eb5905676aaa9b01f870acc7cba1c41ecaa6ebe95979991b3cdde6d7184b29b","clm_49c25e9e4c714aa8c5ff0386c2b77d3f42de2833fc38028ce18331f7420d7917","clm_ab89b3e6f087705482b6c66f6b7487d2acc55f07efc9bd120e7e31a254b1fd25","clm_b102b6fbf0dd73b87495b80b328e6fd09ac258d037bc803aa0c14527fd5e220d","clm_b5778ec096c8aedf70bda1d8e9768c89805135737f4f2341627da89487741738","clm_c4e24fcc04fef0d130e6b37aaa2389bbdbb1304395e66cd59b6820e67fe33d80","clm_f1c91aec83a0e9718c944ae4ea5faa2012761c4654b0ee3e5d2bc82d01b4a720","clm_fc6129a93846711e98cfe1c967e72301cac361acb4a3e2253bf8319653df7d71"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9374c8ebd874686b5edc82805c878cb","id":"pg_6957b22d860c5de19fa94cf1a3c3bfac","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openhands-openhands-readme-md-28464621d879-4cf1a3c3bfac.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1a51db768e475ba89850aa4383e53641"],"title":"OpenHands/OpenHands/README.md @ 28464621d879","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9374c8ebd874686b5edc82805c878cb"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_9612de43cf60e1e4ca02f455466c104378c7b336246d5bc60f3b93508005784b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the changelog follows Keep a Changelog format and the project adheres to Semantic Versioning; npm publishing is automated via a GitHub Actions workflow with OIDC trusted publishing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fae76b886e09b271c63e2a5b69d39679cc5aee3afac8147115dae5d39437917b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The npm package @openhands/agent-canvas exposes subpath exports (browser, conversation, files, settings, sidebar, terminal, i18n) and TypeScript type declarations."}],"claim_ids":["clm_9612de43cf60e1e4ca02f455466c104378c7b336246d5bc60f3b93508005784b","clm_fae76b886e09b271c63e2a5b69d39679cc5aee3afac8147115dae5d39437917b"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:26Z","created_by_operation":"op_e9374c8ebd874686b5edc82805c878cb","id":"pg_97ed4abdbef85fcf94550cbc336d1395","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/openhands-openhands-changelog-md-28464621d879-0cbc336d1395.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_830bc1a1c88e55469ed52ecd316e7a66"],"title":"OpenHands/OpenHands/CHANGELOG.md @ 28464621d879","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:27:26Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e9374c8ebd874686b5edc82805c878cb"}
